# Release and CI/CD pipeline

## Workflows

| Workflow | Trigger | Publishes? |
|----------|---------|------------|
| `ci.yml` | Push/PR to `main` | No — test, lint, GoReleaser snapshot build (`--skip=publish`), SBOM, Trivy |
| `docker.yml` | Dockerfile path changes | No — Hadolint + Dockerfile Trivy config scan |
| `release.yml` | CI success on push to `main` (`workflow_call`); tag `vX.Y.Z` push | Yes — GoReleaser binaries, GH release, GHCR via `dockers_v2` |

Do not change CI checks/workflows just to make failures pass. Fix the code or config causing the failure.

## Push to `main` (snapshot)

- **CI** runs on the push; **Release** runs after test, lint, GoReleaser snapshot build, SBOM, and Trivy succeed (not on PR runs).
- Release force-updates git tag `<latest-v-tag>-snapshot` (e.g. `v0.1.1-snapshot`) and runs `goreleaser release --clean` (not `--snapshot`) so `dockers_v2` can push multi-arch manifests.
- `GORELEASER_CURRENT_TAG` set to that snapshot tag
- GitHub prerelease + module SBOM via GoReleaser (`release.prerelease: auto`, `replace_existing_artifacts`)
- Docker GHCR tag: `ghcr.io/jubblin/omni-kubeconfig:v0.1.1-snapshot` only — **not** `latest` or bare semver
- Cosign + container SBOM after publish; Dockerfile config scan before GoReleaser

```bash
docker pull ghcr.io/jubblin/omni-kubeconfig:v0.1.1-snapshot
```

## Tag `vX.Y.Z` push (release)

- GoReleaser: `release --clean`
- Docker GHCR tags: semver (`0.1.2`) + `major.minor` + `latest`
- Full release assets + signed SBOM bundle

```bash
docker pull ghcr.io/jubblin/omni-kubeconfig:0.1.2
docker pull ghcr.io/jubblin/omni-kubeconfig:latest
```

## When editing `release.yml`

- Keep job-level `permissions` scoped per job (`permissions: {}` at workflow level).
- GoReleaser owns binary build and GHCR push in one job (QEMU + Buildx + GHCR login before `release --clean`).
- Snapshot vs release tagging is driven by `is_snapshot` / `release_tag` / `image_tag` job outputs — do not hardcode version strings in the workflow.
- Tag trigger must be `v[0-9]+.[0-9]+.[0-9]+` so `v*-snapshot` force-pushes do not re-enter Release as a full release.

## Tests in release path

GoReleaser `before` hooks run `go test -buildvcs=false ./...` on every release and snapshot build. Add unit tests for release-related logic (path resolution, tagging helpers) rather than relying on manual Omni credentials in CI.
